Firmware for 'make check-temp60' and 'make check-new-temp60': the 60 Hz mains (SUPPLY_FREQUENCY of
config_system.h) with temperature sensing (configs/temperature.patch, applied too). The scenarios are
the same ones, at 60 Hz (Makefile: out/scn60). A 60 Hz mains gives 26 sample sets per mains cycle
instead of 32, a datalog period of 300 mains cycles instead of 250, and moves the 1-Wire slots
against the ADC conversions.

  PVR_SIM_BUILD=1 sh sim/configs/sim_config.sh NEW          # or without NEW, for check-temp60
  git apply --unidiff-zero sim/configs/temperature.patch sim/configs/supply_60hz.patch
  PLATFORMIO_BUILD_DIR=.pio/build-new-temp60 pio run --project-dir Mk2_3phase_RFdatalog_temp -e basic    # build-temp60 for the old board
  git checkout Mk2_3phase_RFdatalog_temp/config.h Mk2_3phase_RFdatalog_temp/config_system.h
  make -C sim check-new-temp60

